  "content": {
    "id": "p73-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "For the following questions, use a calculator to find the prime factorisation.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p73-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the HCF and LCM of 123 552 and 234 360.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "HCF: 216; LCM: 134 053 920.",
          "worked": "Using a calculator, write the prime factors with matching bases:\n$$\\begin{align*}123\\,552 &= 2^5\\cdot3^3\\cdot5^0\\cdot7^0\\cdot11^1\\cdot13^1\\cdot31^0\\\\234\\,360 &= 2^3\\cdot3^3\\cdot5^1\\cdot7^1\\cdot11^0\\cdot13^0\\cdot31^1\\end{align*}$$\nChoose the smallest powers for the HCF and the largest powers for the LCM.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{HCF}(123\\,552,234\\,360) &= 2^3\\cdot3^3\\cdot5^0\\cdot7^0\\cdot11^0\\cdot13^0\\cdot31^0\\\\\\operatorname{HCF}(123\\,552,234\\,360) &= 216\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(123\\,552,234\\,360) &= 2^5\\cdot3^3\\cdot5^1\\cdot7^1\\cdot11^1\\cdot13^1\\cdot31^1\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(123\\,552,234\\,360) &= 134\\,053\\,920\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p73-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the HCF and LCM of 2760, 4140, and 4830.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "HCF: 690; LCM: 57 960.",
          "worked": "Using a calculator, write the prime factors with matching bases:\n$$\\begin{align*}2760 &= 2^3\\cdot3^1\\cdot5^1\\cdot7^0\\cdot23^1\\\\4140 &= 2^2\\cdot3^2\\cdot5^1\\cdot7^0\\cdot23^1\\\\4830 &= 2^1\\cdot3^1\\cdot5^1\\cdot7^1\\cdot23^1\\end{align*}$$\nChoose the smallest powers across all three numbers for the HCF and the largest powers for the LCM.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{HCF}(2760,4140,4830) &= 2^1\\cdot3^1\\cdot5^1\\cdot7^0\\cdot23^1\\\\\\operatorname{HCF}(2760,4140,4830) &= 690\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(2760,4140,4830) &= 2^3\\cdot3^2\\cdot5^1\\cdot7^1\\cdot23^1\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(2760,4140,4830) &= 57\\,960\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p73-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the HCF and LCM of 1260, 1680, and 2520.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "HCF: 420; LCM: 5040.",
          "worked": "Using a calculator:\n$$\\begin{align*}1260 &= 2^2\\cdot3^2\\cdot5^1\\cdot7^1\\\\1680 &= 2^4\\cdot3^1\\cdot5^1\\cdot7^1\\\\2520 &= 2^3\\cdot3^2\\cdot5^1\\cdot7^1\\end{align*}$$\nChoose the smallest powers across all three numbers for the HCF and the largest powers for the LCM.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{HCF}(1260,1680,2520) &= 2^2\\cdot3^1\\cdot5^1\\cdot7^1\\\\\\operatorname{HCF}(1260,1680,2520) &= 420\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(1260,1680,2520) &= 2^4\\cdot3^2\\cdot5^1\\cdot7^1\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(1260,1680,2520) &= 5040\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      }
    ]
  },
